# Elastic Plan values overscroll

Allow the scrolling values pane to reveal temporary white space beneath the fixed header when pulled down, then spring back into row alignment.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Pulling downward on plan values moves the value rows below their normal top position and reveals white space between them and the fixed header.
- [ ] Releasing the pull springs values smoothly back to their aligned resting position.
- [ ] The fixed plan-name pane, fixed column headers, and meta-header do not move during the pull.
- [ ] The effect works in Default and Custom tables, including expanded custom rows.
- [ ] Normal vertical scrolling and bottom-edge upward overscroll remain unchanged.
- [ ] Horizontal summary/probability navigation remains synchronized and unaffected.
- [ ] Offset normalization cannot leave fixed and value rows permanently misaligned.
- [ ] Automated scroll-state coverage compiles.
- [ ] Focused UI checks pass on a functioning simulator.

## Scope notes

- This supersedes the earlier approach that counteracted all downward overscroll to keep values visually locked.
